1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
"Jesus, thou Son of David,
have mercy on me."

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,800
Many told the blind beggar
to be quiet.

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:06,400
His name was Bartimaeus.

4
00:00:06,860 --> 00:00:09,140
He sat begging by the road
near Jericho.

5
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:12,500
"Son of David" meant
God's promised King.

6
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:14,340
Jesus was on the road
to Jerusalem.

7
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:17,900
He had told His followers
He would be killed there.

8
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:19,920
Would He stop for a beggar?

9
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:22,480
But Bartimaeus shouted
even louder.

10
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:25,500
"Thou Son of David,
have mercy on me."

11
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:28,100
"And Jesus stood still."

12
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:30,400
A whole crowd was moving.

13
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:33,640
He stopped for one man,
and called for him.

14
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:35,600
Bartimaeus threw off his cloak
and came.

15
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:38,400
Jesus asked him what he wanted:

16
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:41,560
"What wilt thou that I
should do unto thee?"

17
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:44,600
"Lord, that I might
receive my sight."

18
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,720
"Go thy way; thy faith
hath made thee whole."

19
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:49,940
He trusted Jesus.

20
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:51,940
Jesus made him well.

21
00:00:52,860 --> 00:00:54,600
At once he could see.

22
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:56,240
He was free to go anywhere.

23
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:58,780
He chose to follow Jesus.

24
00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:01,060
Up the road to Jerusalem.

25
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:04,000
There Jesus died on a cross
for our sins,

26
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,860
for the wrong things
we have done.

27
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:08,260
On the third day,
He rose to life.

28
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:11,700
On His way to die
and rise again,

29
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:16,200
Jesus stood still
for one man.
